From de8cffd3ab8230bfd60fa23e53107cf343577ee0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 13:15:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): detect a pre-existing pre-commit TDD gate and
 defer instead of stacking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An adopter whose repo already gates pre-commit on source/test coupling (e.g.
scripts/check-source-test-coupling.mjs) came out of `forge setup` with TWO TDD
gates blocking the same commit: theirs plus Forge's default-ON rail.tdd_intent.
There was no detection and no reconciliation — the only way out was the
`forge gate disable rail.tdd_intent` workaround.

`forge setup` now detects an existing pre-commit TDD/coupling gate BEFORE wiring
anything and defers to it:
  - no forge-tdd job in a freshly written lefthook.yml
  - no native .git/hooks/pre-commit (pre-push is still wired)
  - rail.tdd_intent turned off in .forge/config.yaml so the hook scripts are
    genuinely inert rather than silently redundant

The deferral is VISIBLE, never a silent skip: setup prints what it detected,
what it did not install, and the one-line `forge gate enable rail.tdd_intent`
opt-in. An explicit rail.tdd_intent setting is never overwritten, so choosing
Forge's gate survives later setup runs.

Detection is by MECHANISM, not a filename list: it enumerates the pre-commit
commands whatever runner is actually installed will execute (lefthook, husky,
the pre-commit framework, a raw .git/hooks/pre-commit) and classifies those
command strings. Forge's own gate is excluded first, so a second `forge setup`
never defers to the gate its own first run installed. A pre-commit mechanism
that cannot be read falls to the safe side — defer and report, since stacking
is the reported failure.

Repos with no existing gate are unaffected: rail.tdd_intent stays default-ON.

Fixes: 7eca930c-e0d5-4866-bbfa-e6ebd0fa100e
Fixes: 2699b234-de35-4308-b0fd-210032acf3c5

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
